1.1 Installation
================

Once accepted by MELPA (https://melpa.org/):

     (use-package org-roam-gt
       :ensure t
       :config
       ;; Optional: load the speed-command menu (transient is bundled with Emacs)
       (require 'org-roam-gt-transient)
       (org-roam-gt-mode 1))

   Or from a local checkout:

     (use-package org-roam-gt
       :load-path "~/.emacs.d/modules/org-roam-gt"
       :config
       (require 'org-roam-gt-transient)
       (org-roam-gt-mode 1))

   To disable, call ‘(org-roam-gt-mode -1)’.  All features are
controlled by the mode and restore their previous state on disable.

   The menu uses ‘transient’, which is bundled with Emacs — nothing
extra to install.  Just ‘(require 'org-roam-gt-transient)’ before
enabling the mode.


