1.4.1 ‘(node TITLE-OR-ID)’
--------------------------

The standard ‘node’ target always prompts, even when you know the
destination in advance.  With ‘org-roam-gt-mode’, passing a string goes
directly to that node by ID or title without prompting.  Passing ‘nil’
still prompts, just as the standard ‘node’ does.

     ;; Go directly to a specific node — no prompt
     '("f" "Farrington tip" entry
       "** %?\n"
       :target (node "mike-farrington-tips")
       :unnarrowed t)

     ;; Prompt the user to pick any node
     '("n" "Note" plain
       "%?"
       :target (node nil)
       :unnarrowed t)


